Q: How to (force to) re-render a functional component? A: <h2>Why are all the answers here so awkward?</h2>
<p>This needs a breath of fresh air.</p>
<pre><code>function MyComponent(){
  const forceUpdate = useReducer(() =&gt; ({}), {})[1]

  return (
    &lt;div onClick={forceUpdate}&gt;
      Click me to refresh
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
}
</code></pre>
<p>Reusable as a custom hook:</p>
<pre><code>function useForceUpdate(): () =&gt; void {
  return useReducer(() =&gt; ({}), {})[1]
}

// later in a component
const forceUpdate = useForceUpdate()
</code></pre>
<p>This works by creating a new object when called, and two objects are never equal <code>({} === {}) === false</code>.</p>
<p><a href="https://gist.github.com/ackvf/39049d109d2097c2b0c273190d0c391c#file-hooks-useforceupdate-ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer">source</a></p>
